{"name":"Motherland","hex":"#bcb667","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"motherland","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The country of one's ancestors.","The country of one's birth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/motherland"}],"entries":[{"title":"Motherland (British TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Motherland is a British sitcom set in West London, which explores the trials of middle-class motherhood. A pilot episode, written by Sharon Horgan, Graham Linehan, Helen Serafinowicz and Holly Walsh, was first broadcast on BBC Two on 6 September 2016 as part of its \"Sitcom Season\". The BBC subsequently ordered a full series of six episodes, the first of which aired on 7 November 2017."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motherland_(British_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q28443707"},{"title":"Motherland (Natalie Merchant album)","blocks":[{"text":"Motherland is the third studio album by Natalie Merchant, released on November 13, 2001, by Elektra Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b0/NatalieMerchant_Motherland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motherland_(Natalie_Merchant_album)","wikidata":"Q3866219"},{"title":"Homeland","blocks":[{"text":"A homeland is a place where a national or ethnic identity has formed. The definition can also mean simply one's country of birth. When used as a proper noun, the Homeland, as well as its equivalents in other languages, often has ethnic nationalist connotations. A homeland may also be referred to as a fatherland, a motherland, or a mother country, depending on the culture and language of the nationality in question."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/La_Libert%C3%A9_guidant_le_peuple_-_Eug%C3%A8ne_Delacroix_-_Mus%C3%A9e_du_Louvre_Peintures_RF_129_-_apr%C3%A8s_restauration_2024.jpg/330px-La_Libert%C3%A9_guidant_le_peuple_-_Eug%C3%A8ne_Delacroix_-_Mus%C3%A9e_du_Louvre_Peintures_RF_129_-_apr%C3%A8s_restauration_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homeland","wikidata":"Q642555"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Bharat_Mata_bronze.jpg/500px-Bharat_Mata_bronze.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Bharat_Mata_bronze.jpg/500px-Bharat_Mata_bronze.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bharat Mata (Mother India) statue accompanied by a lion at Yanam, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABharat_Mata_bronze.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/WWI_postcards_German_and_Austrian_soldiers.jpg/330px-WWI_postcards_German_and_Austrian_soldiers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/WWI_postcards_German_and_Austrian_soldiers.jpg/330px-WWI_postcards_German_and_Austrian_soldiers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Postcard of an Austrian and a German soldier in the First World War with the text \"Shoulder to shoulder, hand in hand, for God, Emperor and Fatherland.\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWWI_postcards_German_and_Austrian_soldiers.jpg"}],"sounds":{"motherland":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/34/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-motherland.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/34/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-motherland.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-motherland.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/3